MAT → M(13) + A(1) + T(20) = 13 + 1 + 20 = 34; 3 + 4 = 7;

BAT → B(2) + A(1) + T(20) = 2 + 1 + 20 = 23; 2 + 3 = 5;

**CAT → C(3) + A(1) + T(20) = 3 + 1 + 20 = 24; 2 + 4 = 6;**

HAT → H(8) + A(1) + T(20) = 8 + 1 + 20 = 29; 2 + 9 = 11;

Hence, '**CAT**' is the odd one among the given alternatives.
